1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,086
Graph RAG helps pharma teams find, connect,

2
00:00:03,086 --> 00:00:05,000
and compare research evidence.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,074
Start by searching PubMed.

4
00:00:07,074 --> 00:00:11,000
Click Ingest to add matching papers.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,767
Papers increase from three to seven.

6
00:00:13,767 --> 00:00:18,000
Section-aware text chunks grow from ten to thirty-two.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,438
Extract entities and PICO fields.

8
00:00:20,438 --> 00:00:24,000
Normalize synonyms to avoid duplicate concept nodes.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,418
Entities grow from eighteen to thirty-two,

10
00:00:26,418 --> 00:00:28,432
edges from thirty-four to eighty-eight,

11
00:00:28,432 --> 00:00:31,000
and communities from five to eight.

12
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,358
The graph view expands from twenty-one to thirty-nine nodes,

13
00:00:34,358 --> 00:00:36,000
connecting studies and concepts.

14
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,156
Hybrid Graph RAG follows study connections, then ranks passages.

15
00:00:40,156 --> 00:00:44,000
This supports cross-paper questions beyond similarity search alone.

16
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,425
Browse normalized concepts in NER,

17
00:00:46,425 --> 00:00:49,000
or compare studies in PICO.

18
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,510
Compare populations, interventions, comparators, and outcomes,

19
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:55,000
then export the evidence.

20
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Check the evidence table and trace citations to source sentences.

21
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,617
R and D can investigate targets.

22
00:01:02,617 --> 00:01:04,797
Clinical development can compare trials,

23
00:01:04,797 --> 00:01:08,000
and medical affairs can prepare cited answers.

24
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,199
Market access teams can compare outcomes.

25
00:01:11,199 --> 00:01:16,000
Safety teams can investigate published findings across studies.

26
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,445
Regulatory reviewers can trace claims to source passages,

27
00:01:19,445 --> 00:01:25,000
helping teams check evidence and identify gaps for further review.

28
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,824
One shared evidence base,

29
00:01:26,824 --> 00:01:30,000
with findings linked to source passages.
